Neverputt, from Neverball 1.6.0 (Robert Kooima and Neverball contributors).

Source: https://neverball.org/neverball-1.6.0.tar.gz
SHA256: 73fe63cca4f96e2d355480d03bc0b2904e83a0abdf65fe8c52db5cc3cca88fa0

Code: GPL version 2 or later; see LICENSE.md and license-GPL-2.0.txt.
Selected putt/ and share/ modules retain their upstream notices and style.
main.c adapts putt/main.c and retains its GPL notice. New native platform
code uses the generated9 root LICENSE; the combined game remains GPL.
Assets remain covered by their upstream licenses and are installed separately.

Local integration:
- Native 6c/mk builds, libdraw/libevent window and input, TinyGL/VirGL rendering.
- System PNG/JPEG readers and libttf replace SDL image/font dependencies.
- Native PCM mixer with original Ogg assets decoded by audio/oggdec.
- Native filesystem, key names, timing, environment and date handling.
- Explicit wire-endian SOL reads/writes, proper prototypes and opaque type
  signatures for the Plan 9 compiler; C stdio string streams own formatting.
- Triangle indices use arrays so element buffers contain no struct padding.
- mapc clamps rounded normal dot products before acos and reports missing
  texture images, retaining finite unit coordinates for default materials.
- Menus expose native window settings and supported rendering options.
  English, mouse and keyboard; no SDL, HMD, fullscreen, reflection or MSAA.
- Accepting the final score with the keyboard returns to the title, matching
  the mouse path; standalone holes may omit background music.

Original data are installed by boot/getneverputt with their complete legal
notices. mk data compiles all Neverputt holes and shared models in the guest.
See README and neverputt(1) for usage and remaining platform limits.
